4. G44-35 — Resource-Bounded ODB Processing (CRITICAL)
Classification: RESOLVED BY DESIGN — subject to implementation and testing (Basis: Established technical reasoning + independent reviewer findings)
4.1 10-Point Control Specification
Exact Threat: Disk, inode, FD, process-table, CPU, or RAM exhaustion via malicious Git repos (50,001+ objects, >25 MiB blobs, fsck warning storms, deep trees, zlib/delta bombs) written to disk before limits are checked.
Trust Assumptions: Kernel enforces setrlimit/setpgid/SIGKILL; C launcher compiles cleanly (-fstack-protector-strong, -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2, overflow-checked uint64_t).
Enforcement Point: Static C Launcher (--bounded-run sub-mode restricted strictly to compiled-in SHA-256-pinned binaries) enforces limits before and during stream reads/writes — never post-write.
Required Input Validation: Pre-run .git/objects raw disk-usage check (<= 512 MiB) + statvfs free-space check (>= 512 MiB) + overflow-checked __builtin_add_overflow on all byte/record counters + strict record-length caps.
Expected Successful Behavior: Producer runs inside isolated process group; C launcher poll()s stdout/stderr pipes, writes bounded output files, calls waitpid(), and propagates exact producer exit code (0).
Failure Behavior: Instant SIGTERM → 500ms → kill(-pgid, SIGKILL) + waitpid() + unlink partial output + distinct non-zero exit (124 timeout, 125 byte cap, 126 record cap, 127 child crash/signal).
Bypass Possibilities: Pre-output zlib/delta CPU/RAM bomb inside git (G44-42), mitigated by RLIMIT_CPU + wall-clock kill + recommended cgroup v2 memory.max; root tampering (RR-10).
Resource-Exhaustion Behavior: Hard kernel RLIMIT_FSIZE (32 MiB) + streaming C byte caps prevent any single capture or cumulative temp usage from filling /tmp.
Required Test Evidence: Tests V35-01–V35-15 (Section 15, NOT RUN).
Remaining Residual Risk: Without cgroup v2 memory.max/pids.max on a shared interactive UID, Go-based gitleaks RAM cannot be capped via RLIMIT_AS (RR-14).
