5.3 Cryptographic Agility & Honest SHA-1 Disclosure
Role Separation: Git sha1 governs object-graph identity (commit/tree/tag/blob OIDs); sha256 governs raw file contents, executables, configs, pubring, and OpenPGP signatures (VALIDSIG F10 ∈ {8,9,10}).
Honest Limitation: No HEAD file content decision relies solely on SHA-1 (every approved file requires matching raw_file_sha256 + git_blob_oid), but SHA-256 in the manifest does NOT eliminate SHA-1 collision risks in Git's internal commit/tree DAG pointers (RR-15, partially mitigated by SHA-1DC in git 2.34.1 and SHA-256+ OpenPGP commit/tag signatures).
Versioned Migration & Anti-Downgrade: Manifest header #PDFSUN-MANIFEST|v1|git_oid=sha1|content_hash=sha256 is mandatory. Future Git sha256 migration requires explicit v2|git_oid=sha256|content_hash=sha256 schema bump; any downgrade (content_hash=sha1, unknown version, or mismatched OID length) fails closed immediately.
5.4 Canonical Manifest Parser (Enforced in C Launcher / Byte-Safe Verifier)
Fixed Schema: Header #PDFSUN-MANIFEST|v1|git_oid=sha1|content_hash=sha256\n, followed by strictly memcmp-sorted 8-field records (v1|<git_mode>|<git_type>|<git_blob_oid>|<raw_file_sha256>|<byte_size>|<fs_perm_policy>|<rel_path>\n).
Hard Caps: MAX_MANIFEST_ENTRIES=10,000, MAX_MANIFEST_BYTES=4 MiB, MAX_LINE_BYTES=1,024, MAX_PATH_BYTES=512.
Anti-Attack Rules: Rejects embedded NULs (0x00), \r, unknown/missing fields, duplicate or unsorted paths, conflicting (blob_oid, raw_file_sha256), non-ASCII bytes (eliminates NFC/NFD Unicode normalization confusion), leading /, //, ., .., .git*, .gitattributes, .gitmodules, and control chars. Hardcoded Layer B 5-file denylist executes independently before manifest authorization.
