9.2 Interruption, SIGKILL, Quarantine & Recovery State Integrity
Signals (SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP): Caught by Bash trap + forwarded via kill(-child_pgid, SIGTERM/SIGKILL); immediately unlinks $TEMP_HOME/.netrc & temp dirs, records state=INTERRUPTED, releases lock, exits non-zero (130/143/129).
SIGKILL / Kernel Panic / OOM Kill (Explicit Honesty): Traps cannot execute. Recovery relies on persistent flock-protected state=IN_PROGRESS detected on the next run: leaked .netrc (if any) is unlinked safely via O_NOFOLLOW, partial staging is never resumed or treated as verified, and Step 16 crashes require manual Owner remote-state reconciliation (G44-44).
Disk Full / Read-Only FS / Failed Unlink / Failed Quarantine: Every write/unlink/rename/mkdir checks rc; failed quarantine exits 92 (never ignored); failed cleanup exits 91 (never reported as success).
Quarantine Integrity (0700 dir, 0400 manifest, <= 4 MiB): Created with full ancestor O_NOFOLLOW walk, records only OIDs/types/classifications/rule IDs/UTC/SHA-256 (zero secret bytes, zero Layer B contents, ANSI/control chars escaped per G44-43). Zero automatic git prune, git gc, or object deletion.
